# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.43 — the RECURSION-CEILING TAINT probe (preserved probe).
#
# WHAT IT ISOLATES
#   The engine's whole-stack recursion ceiling taints the memo floor to 0
#   (`note_recursion_block(0)`), which disables FAILURE memoisation for every
#   enclosing body. This grammar reproduces that defect on ~15 lines:
#
#     * a 5-frame-per-level cascade (expr -> level_a -> level_b -> level_c ->
#       primary -> expr) so N nested parens cost ~5N frames and cross a
#       ceiling of 2000 at N ~ 400;
#     * a 3-way fan-out in `primary` whose alternatives all re-enter `expr` at
#       the SAME position, so losing failure memoisation turns one linear parse
#       into a 3^N search.
#
#   Sub-ceiling input parses in milliseconds; one paren past the ceiling the
#   parse never returns. Same event as the SystemVerilog cliff at 315 -> 320
#   parens, with none of SystemVerilog's size.
#
# HOW TO DRIVE IT
#   python3 -c 'n=380;print("("*n+"1"+")"*n,end="")' > in.txt
#   ./rust/target/debug/ast_pipeline --interpret-parse in.txt \
#       docs/tasks/artifacts/engine_universal_services/deep_nesting_cliff/ceiling_taint_probe.ebnf

@entry: true
probe := expr

expr := level_a
level_a := level_b
level_b := level_c
level_c := primary

#CTRL primary := "(" expr ")" "!"
#CTRL primary := "(" expr ")" "?"
primary := "(" expr ")"
primary := "1"
